{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  DEPRECATED - use sections/section--retail-location.liquid
  ==================================================================
  Renamed on 2026-09-21. Its map depended on a `googlemapapi` theme
  setting that v4 never defined, so it could not render. Presets
  removed so it no longer appears in the section picker; kept only so
  any template still naming it keeps rendering.

  ==================================================================
  RETAIL LOCATION MAIN
  Ported from gs-shopify-v3 sections/retail-location-main.liquid
  ==================================================================
  One store page: title, copy, info / hours / misc blocks, and a map.
  Behind 22 retail location templates, so setting IDs are byte-for-byte
  identical to v3 and all 22 migrate mechanically.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE PAGE BROKE IF A STORE HAD NO COORDINATES
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3 wrote the values straight into JavaScript:

      center: { lat: {{ settings.location_latitude }}, lng: ... }

  With either field blank that is `{ lat: , lng: }` - a SYNTAX ERROR,
  not an empty map. It kills the whole script block, and any other
  inline script that parses after it. Guarded now: no coordinates means
  no map, and the address still renders.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  GOOGLE MAPS LOADED ON EVERY VISIT
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  The Maps JS API plus the marker library is well over 100 KB, loaded
  eagerly on a page whose purpose is an address and opening hours. It is
  now loaded only when the map scrolls into view, and only if
  coordinates exist. Everything above it renders immediately.

  There is also a no-JS fallback link to Google Maps, which v3 lacked.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  DEMO_MAP_ID SHIPPED TO PRODUCTION
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3 used mapId: "DEMO_MAP_ID" - the placeholder from Google's sample
  code. Cloud-based map styling therefore never applied. It is a setting
  now; leave it blank to omit the property entirely.

  The marker variable was still called `beachFlagImg`, also from that
  sample.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  A STORE PAGE THAT STYLED THE MINI CART
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3's stylesheet opened with:

      .nt-mini_cart .mc_body { background: #000 !important; }

  A global rule for a cart component, emitted from a retail location
  section. Same class of leak as the `header h2` rule found in the
  collection filters. Removed.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  OTHER v3 FIXES
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - `hub_link` was a setting that DID NOTHING. The "View Other Stores"
    link was hardcoded to /pages/grunt-style-retail-stores. Wired up,
    with that path as the fallback.
  - .block-size-3 set grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 33%) - two rows for
    three blocks.
  - Each address line was its own `geo:` link. geo: URIs do nothing in
    desktop browsers, and three links to the same destination is noise
    for a screen reader. One clearly labelled maps link now.
  - Inline style="color:#fff!important" on the back link.
  - Hardcoded white text throughout, so the section only worked on a
    dark background. Colours come from the scheme now.
  ==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'gs-retail-location.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  assign lat = s.location_latitude | strip
  assign lng = s.location_longitude | strip

  assign has_coords = false
  if lat != blank and lng != blank
    assign has_coords = true
  endif

  assign hub_url = s.hub_link.url | default: '/pages/grunt-style-retail-stores'

  assign info_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'information' | first
  assign map_query = ''
  if info_block
    capture map_query
      echo info_block.settings.address_line_1
      echo ' '
      echo info_block.settings.address_line_2
    endcapture
  endif
-%}

<div class="gs-retail color-{{ s.color_scheme }}" id="gs-retail-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="page-width">
    <a href="{{ hub_url }}" class="gs-retail__back">
      &lt; {{ s.hub_link_label | default: 'View Other Stores' }}
    </a>

    <h1 class="gs-retail__title">
      {%- if s.title_override != blank -%}{{ s.title_override }}{%- else -%}{{ page.title }}{%- endif -%}
    </h1>

    {%- if s.page_content != blank -%}
      <div class="gs-retail__intro rte">{{ s.page_content }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="gs-retail__details">
      <div class="gs-retail__blocks gs-retail__blocks--{{ section.blocks | size }}">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- case block.type -%}

            {%- when 'information' -%}
              <div class="gs-retail__block gs-retail__block--info" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <h2 class="gs-retail__block-title">
                  {{ block.settings.information_title_override | default: 'Store Info' }}
                </h2>
                <address class="gs-retail__address">
                  {{ block.settings.address_line_1 }}<br>
                  {{ block.settings.address_line_2 }}
                  {%- if block.settings.address_line_3 != blank -%}
                    <br>{{ block.settings.address_line_3 }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </address>

                {%- comment -%}
                  v3 made each address line a geo: link. Those do nothing
                  in a desktop browser, and three links to one place is
                  noise for assistive tech. One labelled link instead.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if has_coords or map_query != blank -%}
                  <a
                    class="gs-retail__maplink"
                    href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query={% if has_coords %}{{ lat }},{{ lng }}{% else %}{{ map_query | url_encode }}{% endif %}"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >
                    {{ s.directions_label | default: 'Get directions' }}
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.phone_no != blank -%}
                  <p class="gs-retail__phone">
                    <strong>Phone:</strong>
                    <a href="tel:{{ block.settings.phone_no | replace: '-', '' | replace: ' ', '' }}">
                      {{ block.settings.phone_no }}
                    </a>
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

            {%- when 'hours' -%}
              <div class="gs-retail__block gs-retail__block--hours" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <h2 class="gs-retail__block-title">
                  {{ block.settings.hours_title_override | default: 'Hours' }}
                </h2>
                <dl class="gs-retail__hours">
                  {%- assign days = 'monday,tuesday,wednesday,thursday,friday,saturday,sunday' | split: ',' -%}
                  {%- for day in days -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign key = 'hours_' | append: day
                      assign value = block.settings[key]
                    -%}
                    {%- if value != blank -%}
                      <div class="gs-retail__hours-row">
                        <dt>{{ day | capitalize }}</dt>
                        <dd>{{ value }}</dd>
                      </div>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </dl>
              </div>

            {%- when 'misc' -%}
              <div class="gs-retail__block gs-retail__block--misc" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- if block.settings.misc_title != blank -%}
                  <h2 class="gs-retail__block-title">{{ block.settings.misc_title }}</h2>
                {%- endif -%}
                <div class="rte">{{ block.settings.misc_textarea }}</div>
              </div>

          {%- endcase -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- if has_coords -%}
        <div
          class="gs-retail__map"
          id="gs-retail-map-{{ section.id }}"
          data-retail-map
          data-lat="{{ lat }}"
          data-lng="{{ lng }}"
          data-zoom="{{ s.map_zoom | default: 12 }}"
          {% if s.map_id != blank %}data-map-id="{{ s.map_id }}"{% endif %}
          {% if s.marker_image != blank %}data-marker="{{ s.marker_image | image_url: width: 240 }}"{% endif %}
          role="img"
          aria-label="{{ s.map_aria_label | default: 'Map showing the store location' }}"
        >
          <noscript>
            <a
              class="gs-retail__maplink"
              href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query={{ lat }},{{ lng }}"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              {{ s.directions_label | default: 'Get directions' }}
            </a>
          </noscript>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- if has_coords and settings.googlemapapi != blank -%}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var el = document.getElementById('gs-retail-map-{{ section.id }}');
      if (!el) return;

      var loaded = false;

      function loadMaps() {
        if (loaded) return;
        loaded = true;

        var script = document.createElement('script');
        script.src =
          'https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key={{ settings.googlemapapi }}&v=weekly&libraries=maps,marker&loading=async&callback=gsRetailInit{{ section.id }}';
        script.async = true;
        script.onerror = function () {
          el.classList.add('is-failed');
        };
        document.head.appendChild(script);
      }

      window['gsRetailInit{{ section.id }}'] = function () {
        var lat = parseFloat(el.dataset.lat);
        var lng = parseFloat(el.dataset.lng);
        if (isNaN(lat) || isNaN(lng)) return;

        var options = {
          center: { lat: lat, lng: lng },
          zoom: parseInt(el.dataset.zoom, 10) || 12
        };
        // v3 shipped Google's DEMO_MAP_ID, so cloud styling never applied.
        if (el.dataset.mapId) options.mapId = el.dataset.mapId;

        var map = new google.maps.Map(el, options);

        if (el.dataset.marker && google.maps.marker) {
          var img = document.createElement('img');
          img.src = el.dataset.marker;
          img.alt = '';
          img.style.width = '120px';
          new google.maps.marker.AdvancedMarkerElement({
            map: map,
            position: { lat: lat, lng: lng },
            content: img
          });
        } else {
          new google.maps.Marker({ map: map, position: { lat: lat, lng: lng } });
        }
      };

      // Over 100 KB of Maps JS for an address and opening hours. Load it
      // when it is actually about to be seen.
      if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(
          function (entries) {
            entries.forEach(function (entry) {
              if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
              io.disconnect();
              loadMaps();
            });
          },
          { rootMargin: '200px 0px' }
        );
        io.observe(el);
      } else {
        loadMaps();
      }
    })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Retail main (deprecated)",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "gs-retail-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_override", "label": "Page title override", "info": "Leave blank to use the page title." },
    {
      "type": "page",
      "id": "hub_link",
      "label": "Main hub page",
      "info": "Controls the 'View Other Stores' link. In v3 this setting existed but was never applied - the link was hardcoded."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hub_link_label", "label": "Hub link text", "default": "View Other Stores" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "page_content", "label": "Page content" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Map" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "location_latitude",
      "label": "Latitude",
      "info": "Leave both coordinates blank to hide the map. In v3 a blank value broke the page."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "location_longitude", "label": "Longitude" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "map_zoom", "label": "Zoom", "min": 8, "max": 18, "step": 1, "default": 12 },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "map_id",
      "label": "Google Cloud map ID",
      "info": "For cloud-based map styling. v3 shipped Google's DEMO_MAP_ID, so styling never applied. Leave blank to omit."
    },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "marker_image", "label": "Map marker image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "map_aria_label", "label": "Map description", "default": "Map showing the store location" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "directions_label", "label": "Directions link text", "default": "Get directions" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colors" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-4" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "name": "Store Information",
      "type": "information",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "information_title_override", "label": "Title override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "address_line_1", "label": "Address line 1", "default": "900 Broadway Street" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "address_line_2", "label": "Address line 2", "default": "San Antonio, TX 78215" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "address_line_3", "label": "Address line 3" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "phone_no", "label": "Phone number" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Store Hours",
      "type": "hours",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_title_override", "label": "Title override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_monday", "label": "Monday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_tuesday", "label": "Tuesday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_wednesday", "label": "Wednesday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_thursday", "label": "Thursday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_friday", "label": "Friday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_saturday", "label": "Saturday" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "hours_sunday", "label": "Sunday" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Misc Details",
      "type": "misc",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "misc_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Parking" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "misc_textarea", "label": "Text", "default": "<p>This is some text</p>" }
      ]
    }
  ]}
{% endschema %}
